<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dong Yi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 203 BCE</span> · Also known as King of Di</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dong Yi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> commander who urged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-han">Zhang Han</a> to surrender to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> in 207 BCE. In the division of 206 BCE Xiang Yu made him King of Di in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-qins">Three Qins</a>. He surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> within months, later rejoined Xiang Yu and killed himself after a defeat by Han forces around 203 BCE.</p></div>
